## 1. Introduction and Scope Changes

Study Tracker Desktop is a personal, offline, single-user desktop application that gamifies studying: users log study sessions, earn XP for completed 10-minute blocks, win daily Bronze/Silver/Gold medals, maintain streaks, keep free-text notes, and review statistics — all stored locally in JSON.

The delivered application implements every core rule confirmed in the initial requirements document (XP rate, medal thresholds, day attribution, week definition, streak rules, save/backup/versioning behavior, asset fallbacks, packaging). In addition, the following scope changes were made during implementation:

| Change | Description |
|---|---|
| **[UPDATED] Navigation model** | The persistent *bottom* navigation bar with four destinations became a persistent **left sidebar** with **five** destinations: Home, Calendar, Notes, Statistics, Settings. UI-1's "side navigation is acceptable only if it preserves the same simplicity" clause is exercised. |
| **[NEW] Notes feature** | A dedicated Notes screen and data type (titled free-text notes, optionally attached to a calendar day). This partially supersedes initial FUT-2-style out-of-scope items by adding a note-taking capability (not subject categorization). |
| **[NEW] Study stopwatch** | A real-time digital stopwatch in the sidebar that can automatically log a completed run as a custom session. This was listed as out of scope in the initial document (FUT-3 "Real-time study timer") and is now an implemented, required feature. |
| **[UPDATED] Platform target** | Primary distribution remains a standalone Windows executable, but the app is explicitly **cross-platform at source level** (macOS/Linux supported via `platformdirs`); README documents running from source on any OS. NFR-1 is relaxed accordingly. |
| **[UPDATED] Editing policy** | Session editing remains out of scope (A-8 holds). However, **note editing is fully supported** (create/edit/delete notes), so the blanket "no editing" phrasing applies only to sessions. |
| **[UPDATED] Persistence naming** | The concrete save-file names differ from early planning docs: `study_tracker_save.json` with backup `study_tracker_save.backup.json` and `.corrupt[.N]` quarantine suffixes, located in the per-user app-data directory (`APP_SLUG = "StudyTrackerDesktop"`). |
| **[NEW] Performance engineering layer** | An incremental daily-aggregate index and lazy screen construction were added specifically to satisfy the ≥10,000-session responsiveness requirement (NFR-9), with an automated budget gate (`scripts/perf_check.py`). |
| **[NEW] Build pipeline** | A scripted Windows release pipeline (`run_build.ps1` + `study_tracker.spec`) that gates shipping on the test suite and the performance check. |

