## 3. Confirmed Assumptions and Binding Decisions (Revised)

All initial assumptions A-1 through A-13 remain binding and implemented as stated (verified in `app/constants.py` and the core engines). New/updated decisions:

| ID | Decision | Consequence / Rule |
|---|---|---|
| A-1 … A-13 | *(unchanged)* | XP = 10 per completed 10-min block; partial blocks award nothing; midnight-crossing sessions attributed wholly to start day; custom duration 5 min–12 h; default save in per-user app-data folder; week = Monday–Sunday; qualifying day = ≥10 minutes; sessions deletable but not editable; manual load replaces after confirmation; default theme dark; highest-medal-per-day counting; overlaps allowed; local clock trusted. |
| **A-14 [NEW]** | Notes are first-class persisted data alongside sessions. | Stored in the same JSON save file (`notes` array), covered by autosave, backup, atomic write, and recovery flows. |
| **A-15 [NEW]** | Note limits are fixed: title ≤ 120 characters, body ≤ 100,000 characters. | Values are truncated defensively on load; a note with neither title nor body text is rejected with a friendly message. |
| **A-16 [NEW]** | A stopwatch stop logs a session only when elapsed time ≥ 10 minutes (±0.25 s floating-point slack), rounded **down** to whole 10-minute steps. | Shorter stops preserve the reading so the run can be resumed; Reset always returns the display to zero without logging. Logged runs use the normal custom-session validation path. |
| **A-17 [NEW]** | Stopwatch timing uses a monotonic clock, not wall-clock deltas. | Display accuracy survives delayed Tk callbacks; system clock changes do not distort a running measurement. |
| **A-18 [NEW]** | Derived views are backed by an incrementally maintained daily index. | Adding/deleting a session updates only the affected day's aggregate; stats/calendar/home read the index. Deletion recomputes day XP from remaining sessions (partial-block rounding makes XP non-additive). |
| **A-19 [UPDATED vs A-5/A-13/NFR-1]** | Cross-platform data location. | Default save directory resolves via `platformdirs.user_data_dir`: `%APPDATA%\StudyTrackerDesktop`-style per-user location on Windows and platform-standard locations on macOS/Linux. Windows remains the packaging/distribution target. |
| **A-20 [NEW]** | Screens are constructed lazily on first visit. | Startup does not build the calendar grid, notes list, or stats cards until navigated to; unvisited screens are skipped by global refresh broadcasts. |

