## 5. User Interface Structure (As Built)

### 5.1 Overall layout

One main window (default 900×640, minimum 700×520) divided into:

- **Left sidebar (fixed ≈210 px):** brand block (app icon + name + tagline), separator, five navigation buttons (icon when available + always-visible text label), then at the bottom: the **Study Stopwatch widget** packed above the version label (`v1.0.0`).
- **Content area:** exactly one primary screen visible at a time (UI-2 preserved), raised via `tkraise()`; screens are created lazily on first visit (A-20).

Home remains the default screen after launch (UI-3). Active nav item is highlighted with the accent-blue pill; inactive items use theme-appropriate grey text.

### 5.2 Screens

| Screen | Purpose | Main actions |
|---|---|---|
| Home / Log Study | Today summary card (time, XP, medal badge, progress bar toward next medal) | Preset buttons (30 m / 1 h / 2 h, responsive row/grid layout); open custom-session modal |
| Calendar | Monday-first month grid with medal-icon and note-count markers per day | Prev/Next month, "Today" button, click day → Day Details modal |
| Notes **[NEW]** | List + detail panes (fixed 2:3 split) with search and New-note toolbar | Create, edit, delete, open attached day |
| Statistics | Colour-coded summary-card sections: Time, XP earned, Streaks, Medal days, Activity | Read-only review |
| Settings | Appearance card, Data management card, Data status card | Theme toggle, Save now, Load from file |

### 5.3 Dialogs and widgets

| Component | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| Custom session dialog | Modal; separate hours/minutes fields; inline friendly validation (ERR-1..ERR-4). |
| Day Details dialog | Modal (600×560); date header, totals + medal badge, scrollable session rows with per-session delete (confirm first), notes section listing attached notes with "+ Add note" and edit routes; friendly empty states for both sessions and notes. |
| Note editor dialog | Modal (520×460); title field, body textbox, optional day; routes through AppState so all screens refresh; rejects blank notes with a friendly message. |
| Confirm dialog (`ask_yes_no`) | Generic modal yes/no used before destructive/replacement actions (delete session, delete note, replace data on manual load). |
| Message/error dialogs | Non-technical friendly notices used throughout (save failures, recovery notices, stopwatch auto-log confirmation). |
| MedalBadge | Shows medal PNG when the asset exists; otherwise coloured text ("Bronze"/"Silver"/"Gold"); empty when no medal. |
