| StopwatchWidget **[NEW]** | See §6.8. |

### 5.4 Visual theme system **[UPDATED]**

All GUI colours are centralised in `app/gui/theme` tokens (accent blue `#2b6cb0`, neutral, danger, card/border surfaces, muted text, time-blue, XP-gold, medal colours) defined as `(light, dark)` tuples resolved per appearance mode. Dark mode remains the default (A-10). Specific documented behaviours:

- Calendar tiles are light-grey-tinted in light mode and lighter navy in dark mode; today's tile uses the **same blue accent** as the header "Today" button; selected day gets an accent outline ring. Tile contents use a uniform composite structure so the date number sits at identical vertical position whether or not the day carries a medal/note marker.
- Date-number colours follow live appearance-mode switches (an appearance watcher recolours rendered cells immediately).
- Notes rows: selected rows get a tinted accent background per theme; unselected titles use exactly the body-text colour pair.
- Symmetric content insets across all screens (equal left/right outer gaps).

UI-14 (friendly empty states), UI-15 (offline-only), and UI-16 (usable at typical desktop size) are satisfied; empty-state helper shows the `empty_state` asset when present plus a friendly message.

