## 6. Functional Requirements

## 6.1 Study Sessions and XP

FR-1 … FR-16 from the initial document are implemented as written. Notable implementation specifics:

| ID | Requirement (as built) |
|---|---|
| FR-1 | Presets `(30, 60, 120)` minutes defined in constants with labels "30 minutes / 1 hour / 2 hours"; buttons log immediately via `log_preset_session(source="preset")`. |
| FR-2–FR-5 | Custom dialog validates through `Session.validate_custom_inputs(hours, minutes)` returning `(total_minutes, friendly_error_or_None)`; hours 0–12, minutes 0–59, total 5 min–12 h enforced. |
| FR-6 | `Session.create()` stamps end = current local time (or injected `now` for tests), start = end − duration, plus `created_at_local` and `source` ("preset"/"custom"). Naive local datetimes throughout. |
| FR-7/FR-8 | Attribution property `Session.day = start_local.date()`; no splitting anywhere in the codebase. |
| FR-9–FR-11 | XP = `(duration // 10) * settings.xp_per_10_minutes`; integer-only; rate persisted in settings without a UI editor. |
| FR-12 | Medal/time engines use raw `duration_minutes`, independent of XP rounding. |
| FR-13–FR-15 | Delete flows through `AppState.delete_session` → index update → autosave → listener broadcast refreshing every built screen (Home, Calendar, Stats, Notes, open Day Details). |
| FR-16 | No overlap detection. |
| **[UPDATED]** | Manual-load validation additionally rejects nonsensical persisted durations (≤0 or >24 h) by skipping those records rather than crashing (see ERR-10). |

