## 6.4 Statistics Screen

FR-38 … FR-52 implemented via the pure `compute_stats` engine, which accepts an optional pre-built `day_index` (Part L optimization) and optional notes collection. The Stats screen renders colour-coded `SummaryCard`s grouped into sections: Study time (Today/Week/Month/Lifetime), XP earned (same four periods), Streaks (current/longest, "N day(s)" pluralisation), Medal days (Bronze/Silver/Gold, highest-per-day), and Activity (total sessions, active days, average daily time, **total notes [NEW]**). A friendly empty hint appears below the cards when no sessions exist. All period math uses local dates and start-day attribution; week bounds are Monday–Sunday (`week_bounds`), month bounds first-to-last day (`month_bounds`).

## 6.5 Save, Load, Backup, and Versioning

FR-53 … FR-75 implemented by `app/persistence` + `AppState`, with these concrete behaviours:

| ID | Requirement (as built) |
|---|---|
| FR-53/FR-54 | UTF-8 JSON (`indent=2`, `ensure_ascii=False`) in `platformdirs.user_data_dir("StudyTrackerDesktop")`; file names `study_tracker_save.json` / `study_tracker_save.backup.json`; quarantine suffix `.corrupt` (numbered `.corrupt.N` on collision). |
| FR-55/FR-56 | First run creates the directory and an empty-default save silently; startup loads automatically (`AppState.load_startup` invoked by `MainWindow.run_startup_load`). |
| FR-57 | Autosave fires inside every mutating operation (session add/delete, note create/update/delete, theme change, manual load commit) via `_mark_dirty_and_save()`. |
| FR-58 | `WM_DELETE_WINDOW` handler flushes when `dirty` is set; a failed final save shows a friendly error before quitting. |
| FR-59/FR-60 | Settings provides "Save now" (immediate write + confirmation message) and "Load from file" (JSON file chooser). Cancelling the chooser changes nothing. |
| FR-61–FR-63 | Three-step manual load flow: (1) parse+validate selected file **without touching current data**; failure → friendly message, data unchanged; (2) explicit "Replace current data?" confirmation noting a backup will be made; cancel → unchanged; (3) backup current default save, then atomically replace with loaded dataset; success/failure reported with friendly messages. |
| FR-64–FR-65 | One last-known-good backup beside the default save; created before manual-load overwrite. Backup failures never block normal saving (atomic write alone protects the main file). |
| FR-66–FR-69 | Startup recovery sequence: missing file → silent empty first-run; corrupt default → try backup → on success recover with notice and quarantine the bad default; both unusable → start empty, quarantine both files, notify. Corrupt files are never silently deleted. |
| FR-70–FR-72 | `schema_version` written (currently 1); missing version treated as 1; version > supported raises `FutureSchemaError` → the file is never overwritten, the app starts with empty data and shows the "newer version" notice. |
| FR-73/FR-74 | Settings (`theme`, `xp_per_10_minutes`) persisted; `Settings.sanitized()` coerces invalid values back to defaults (dark / 10). |
| FR-75 | Atomic save: write temp file → flush + `fsync` → `os.replace`; temp cleanup on failure; in-memory state untouched on disk errors (ERR-13). |

