## 9. Error Handling and Edge Cases

ERR-1 … ERR-17 from the initial document are implemented as specified (friendly validation strings from `Session.validate_*`, confirmation dialogs, silent first-run creation, backup recovery with notice, quarantine preservation, partial-record skipping with the "some sessions could not be loaded" warning, future-schema refusal to overwrite, asset text fallbacks, disk-write errors keeping memory intact, clock/DST stability, friendly empty states, and exception-swallowing refresh guards). Additional behaviours introduced with the new features:

| ID | Scenario | Required Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| ERR-18 **[NEW]** | Stopwatch auto-log fails validation unexpectedly. | Show the engine's friendly message; do not lose the elapsed display semantics defined in SW-5/SW-6. |
| ERR-19 **[NEW]** | Note submitted with empty title and empty body. | Friendly rejection ("Give your note a title or some text before saving."); nothing stored. |
| ERR-20 **[NEW]** | Note/day references point to a note id that no longer exists (stale UI). | Friendly "could not be found" message; no crash. |
| ERR-21 **[NEW]** | Save payload contains duplicate session/note ids or malformed individual records. | Skip duplicates/invalid records, warn once with the partial-load message, load everything else. |
| ERR-22 **[NEW]** | Note text fields arrive non-string or oversized in a hand-edited save file. | Coerce to string and clamp to limits (`sanitize_text`); never crash. |
| ERR-23 **[NEW]** | Any screen's `refresh()` throws. | Exception is contained per-screen; other screens continue refreshing; app stays alive. |
| ERR-24 **[NEW]** | Running without CustomTkinter installed from source. | `main.py` exits with a clear install-instruction message instead of a traceback. |

