## 10. Save File Data Schema (As Implemented)

Schema version remains **1**; derived data is still computed at runtime (DATA-1 … DATA-6 hold). The implemented top-level structure adds the `notes` array:

```json
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "created_at": "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS",
  "updated_at": "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS",
  "settings": { "theme": "dark", "xp_per_10_minutes": 10 },
  "sessions": [
    {
      "id": "<uuid>",
      "start_local": "<ISO local datetime>",
      "end_local": "<ISO local datetime>",
      "duration_minutes": 60,
      "created_at_local": "<ISO local datetime>",
      "source": "preset | custom"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "<uuid>",
      "title": "…",
      "body": "…",
      "day": "YYYY-MM-DD | null",
      "created_at_local": "<ISO local datetime>",
      "updated_at_local": "<ISO local datetime>"
    }
  ]
}
```

Rules implemented by `dataset_to_payload` / `validate_payload`:

- Datetimes serialise as ISO-style local naive strings via `format_dt`; `updated_at` is refreshed on every successful save.
- `notes` is optional on read: a missing key loads as an empty list (forward/backward tolerance); a non-list `notes` value marks the file corrupt.
- Note `day` stores a plain ISO date (datetime strings are accepted and reduced to their date part); unparsable day values yield an undated note rather than a rejected record.
- Note timestamps fall back sensibly (missing created ← updated ← now; missing updated ← created).
- Session parsing: `id` must be a non-empty string; `start_local` must parse; `duration_minutes` must be an integer in (0, 1440]; `end_local` optional (derived as start + duration); `created_at_local` optional (defaults to end); unknown `source` values default to `"preset"`.
- Settings sanitising: invalid/missing theme → `dark`; invalid/negative XP rate → `10`.
- Files whose overall structure is unusable raise typed errors mapped to friendly messages; future `schema_version` raises `FutureSchemaError` and is never overwritten.

